WEBVTT

00:00:05.424 --> 00:00:08.325
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:11.897
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:13.956
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.930
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:23.342
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.342 --> 00:00:25.469
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.245 --> 00:00:30.272
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:31.984 --> 00:00:34.754
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.754 --> 00:00:37.382
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.656 --> 00:00:41.251
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:47.359
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.869
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:53.066
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:57.076
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.076 --> 00:01:01.137
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.010
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.787 --> 00:01:09.277
Let's go!

00:01:12.525 --> 00:01:15.983
SHINY! HAPPY!
(DEADLY] GERMS

00:01:29.842 --> 00:01:30.433
Yes?

00:01:30.609 --> 00:01:31.303
Harumi?

00:01:31.644 --> 00:01:32.201
Yes.

00:01:32.645 --> 00:01:34.010
Prepare to capture Tylor.

00:01:34.847 --> 00:01:38.544
What's wrong? Tylor hasn't
seduced you, has he?

00:01:38.751 --> 00:01:41.652
No! The captain
would never do that!

00:01:41.921 --> 00:01:45.482
Pardon, but are we capturing him
to be executed on the Melva?

00:01:45.658 --> 00:01:47.093
That's no concern of yours.

00:01:47.093 --> 00:01:47.923
But...

00:01:48.194 --> 00:01:52.062
Fool! An android shouldn't
care about such things!

00:01:52.398 --> 00:01:54.366
An android has no
use for emotions!

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.131
No use for emotions!

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.234
Is that clear?

00:02:00.372 --> 00:02:03.671
Begin the mission for which you've
been preparing. That is all.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:04.801
Acknowledged.

00:02:14.453 --> 00:02:15.977
I am an android.

00:02:16.822 --> 00:02:20.155
And so I cannot disobey
a living person's orders.

00:02:22.761 --> 00:02:24.023
A vitamin deficiency?

00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:26.829
And getting this
injection will cure me?

00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:27.723
Yes, sir.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:28.998
Well, then...

00:02:29.835 --> 00:02:31.769
Just be gentle with me, okay?

00:02:32.138 --> 00:02:33.105
Aye, aye, sir.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.099
Captain?

00:02:36.408 --> 00:02:39.775
You know I'm a
Raalgon spy, right?

00:02:39.945 --> 00:02:42.345
Sure, I know that. So what?

00:02:42.515 --> 00:02:47.612
Don't you worry that this injection
I'm giving you might be poison?

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.211
What's brought this up?
Of course it isn't!

00:02:50.523 --> 00:02:54.084
I mean, you'd never
try to kill me, right?

00:02:55.494 --> 00:02:56.859
Well? Aren't I right?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.862
Yes, sir. Just as you say.

00:03:15.548 --> 00:03:19.348
Shia Has... A good commander
or a good subordinate.

00:03:20.486 --> 00:03:23.478
If you could have only one,
which would you choose?

00:03:23.656 --> 00:03:26.318
A good commander, of course.

00:03:27.226 --> 00:03:30.354
You're saying good subordinates
are unnecessary in battle?

00:03:30.563 --> 00:03:34.556
No, sir. A good commander makes
his subordinates good as well.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.391
Very well. Go. Go and see.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.433
Yes, sir. I shall indeed.

00:03:45.878 --> 00:03:46.936
She has much to learn.

00:04:03.329 --> 00:04:05.160
Passing point R-1.

00:04:05.431 --> 00:04:07.296
Navigation system, nominal.

00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:11.965
All systems go! Guess we'll be
meeting up with the fleet soon.

00:04:12.938 --> 00:04:15.600
And saying goodbye to Harumi.

00:04:15.941 --> 00:04:16.999
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:17.443 --> 00:04:19.741
Huh? What about Harumi?

00:04:39.965 --> 00:04:43.059
WHAT?!
Harumi's leaving the ship?!

00:04:43.269 --> 00:04:45.760
What are you so
surprised about, Captain?

00:04:45.971 --> 00:04:49.907
A female med tech gets transferred
to a rear line military hospital...

00:04:49.975 --> 00:04:54.139
...if she serves for more than
2000 hours aboard a ship.

00:04:54.446 --> 00:04:56.209
With a promotion, of course.

00:04:56.649 --> 00:04:59.015
She's served here over
the required time.

00:04:59.285 --> 00:05:01.480
She'll most likely
get orders to transfer.

00:05:02.254 --> 00:05:04.654
This is the first
I've heard about it!

00:05:05.291 --> 00:05:07.384
There's a lot you don't know.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.627
Exactly.

00:05:09.261 --> 00:05:12.321
The Marines are really
excited about this.

00:05:12.665 --> 00:05:15.964
They said they're trying to
score with her before she leaves.

00:05:25.244 --> 00:05:26.404
Harumi!

00:05:32.518 --> 00:05:33.712
Where'd she go?

00:05:35.688 --> 00:05:37.622
Something wrong, Captain?

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.657
Harumi!

00:05:40.326 --> 00:05:41.623
The others just told me.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.988
You'd never leave the
Soyokaze, would you?

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:49.728
What's brought this up?

00:05:53.305 --> 00:05:54.033
I know!

00:05:55.007 --> 00:05:57.840
Think about it.
You're a spy, right?

00:05:58.177 --> 00:06:01.943
If they send you to the rear,
you can't get any information.

00:06:02.648 --> 00:06:04.878
R- Right... But...

00:06:07.019 --> 00:06:10.887
Don't worry, sir.
I'll always be at your side.

00:06:11.724 --> 00:06:13.749
No matter where you may go.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.120
Really?! Then let's
go to a hot spring resort!

00:06:17.363 --> 00:06:21.026
I'd love to take everyone
here to one and just relax.

00:06:26.038 --> 00:06:28.165
Captain, if you were...

00:06:29.675 --> 00:06:32.769
If you were ever taken prisoner
by the Raalgon Empire...

00:06:33.379 --> 00:06:35.210
...I'd protect you.

00:06:37.049 --> 00:06:40.712
I wonder if they have hot
springs in the Raalgon Empire?

00:06:45.357 --> 00:06:49.885
But the Empire kills all of
its prisoners, doesn't it?

00:06:53.065 --> 00:06:54.259
No, Captain!

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.294
Even if it meant having to die,
I wouldn't let that happen!

00:07:02.074 --> 00:07:03.336
Glad to hear it!

00:07:03.709 --> 00:07:06.735
Then a trip to a Raalgon hot
spring wouldn't be so bad.

00:07:07.379 --> 00:07:09.313
That's what I'd like to say...

00:07:09.381 --> 00:07:11.406
...but I'd rather stay
here on the Soyokaze.

00:07:12.117 --> 00:07:15.280
It's fun being the captain,
and besides...

00:07:15.788 --> 00:07:18.222
I like being here
with Mr. Yamamoto...

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.656
...and Yuriko and
the rest of the crew.

00:07:20.793 --> 00:07:22.226
C- Captain...

00:07:22.795 --> 00:07:26.094
Somehow, fate made
all of us friends.

00:07:27.766 --> 00:07:31.065
And even though you're a
Raalgon spy, Harumi...

00:07:31.136 --> 00:07:33.001
...you're a part
of the Soyokaze, too.

00:07:39.311 --> 00:07:43.077
Well, now that I'm not worried
anymore, I'm really hungry.

00:07:43.148 --> 00:07:45.116
Want to get something
to eat, Harumi?

00:07:45.517 --> 00:07:47.144
No, I...

00:07:47.352 --> 00:07:51.550
Oh. Well, see you.
Wonder what I should have?

00:07:57.262 --> 00:07:58.354
I...

00:08:00.165 --> 00:08:01.462
I've betrayed them all...

00:08:05.137 --> 00:08:06.365
It's so cold...

00:08:08.474 --> 00:08:09.668
Damn it!

00:08:14.346 --> 00:08:16.007
Yumi, help me.

00:08:16.515 --> 00:08:19.814
Mr. Kojiro... I can't breathe!

00:08:20.452 --> 00:08:21.976
Stay away from me.

00:08:22.488 --> 00:08:24.888
But, it's so cold.

00:08:25.724 --> 00:08:28.659
Mr. Kojiro,
don't be so cold to us!

00:08:29.027 --> 00:08:32.394
Damn. Now I'm getting a fever.

00:08:36.401 --> 00:08:37.698
What's wrong with you guys?!

00:08:55.888 --> 00:08:58.823
This is the virus that's
causing the epidemic.

00:08:58.891 --> 00:09:03.794
70% of the crew has
come down with it.

00:09:03.862 --> 00:09:05.830
It'll eventually spread
to everyone, won't it?

00:09:05.898 --> 00:09:11.859
Yeah... The thing is, I think
it was artificially created.

00:09:12.504 --> 00:09:13.562
What do you mean?!

00:09:14.239 --> 00:09:17.174
I'm saying there's
a possibility that...

00:09:17.242 --> 00:09:19.836
...a Raalgon spy got
on board the Soyokaze...

00:09:19.912 --> 00:09:25.475
...and intentionally
released this virus.

00:09:25.551 --> 00:09:26.415
A spy?

00:09:37.596 --> 00:09:41.896
Harumi... I'm sorry...
Some water, please...

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:42.825
Yes, sir.

00:09:49.575 --> 00:09:51.736
Thank you, Harumi...

00:09:52.277 --> 00:09:55.178
You're the Soyokaze's
own Florence Nightingale...

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:01.978
I'm... I'm glad
you're all right...

00:10:02.254 --> 00:10:03.915
No, please...

00:10:06.925 --> 00:10:08.290
Harumi...

00:10:09.261 --> 00:10:10.193
Harumi!

00:10:10.963 --> 00:10:11.725
Harumi!

00:10:16.635 --> 00:10:18.330
Give me some water, too...

00:10:19.304 --> 00:10:19.998
Yes.

00:10:26.478 --> 00:10:30.107
Why?! Why do
I feel this pain?

00:10:32.951 --> 00:10:34.646
I'm an android...

00:10:36.622 --> 00:10:39.785
I'm a spy... Why?!

00:11:00.345 --> 00:11:02.609
Doctor, can you
make a vaccine?

00:11:03.115 --> 00:11:05.413
We're dealing with
an unknown virus here.

00:11:05.484 --> 00:11:08.009
Producing a vaccine
will take time.

00:11:08.353 --> 00:11:10.287
And how long do we have?

00:11:10.656 --> 00:11:12.248
A day, maybe.

00:11:12.991 --> 00:11:15.357
Not enough time to
make a vaccine, huh?

00:11:24.369 --> 00:11:26.837
Looks like things
just got a lot worse.

00:11:26.972 --> 00:11:28.064
You said it.

00:11:32.778 --> 00:11:35.770
What do you want?!
We're busy here!

00:11:36.381 --> 00:11:41.114
So, how do you like the synthetic
virus our agent set loose?

00:11:41.386 --> 00:11:43.650
So, I was right about that!

00:11:46.391 --> 00:11:47.756
You know what this is?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:48.992
No, what?

00:11:49.661 --> 00:11:52.152
It's the vaccine
for the virus.

00:11:52.397 --> 00:11:55.764
The vaccine! Then hurry
up and give it to us!

00:11:57.402 --> 00:11:59.836
You can have it. However...

00:12:00.005 --> 00:12:00.972
However?

00:12:03.375 --> 00:12:05.070
Give them the captain?!

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.340
Yeah. Their condition for
giving us the vaccine...

00:12:08.413 --> 00:12:12.076
...is that we have to
exchange the captain for it.

00:12:13.085 --> 00:12:14.518
But, what about the captain?

00:13:05.103 --> 00:13:06.035
Harumi.

00:13:06.471 --> 00:13:10.703
I want to apologize to everyone
on board for what I did, Captain.

00:13:11.042 --> 00:13:13.101
This must be hard for you, too.

00:13:13.745 --> 00:13:15.440
Care to take me
to your hot spring?

00:13:16.481 --> 00:13:17.948
Yes, Captain.

00:13:22.487 --> 00:13:26.082
We'll have to capture them
and take the vaccine!

00:13:26.324 --> 00:13:28.155
But, in your condition...

00:13:28.493 --> 00:13:29.858
We have no choice!

00:13:32.764 --> 00:13:33.492
Look!

00:13:40.172 --> 00:13:42.640
Wha- What's Harumi doing there?

00:13:43.175 --> 00:13:48.169
Is she?! Is she the Raalgon spy
who released the virus on board?!

00:13:49.181 --> 00:13:53.277
It can't be! Harumi, a spy?!

00:14:09.201 --> 00:14:11.829
Your subordinates
aren't very good.

00:14:13.071 --> 00:14:15.505
If you want to live, throw down
your weapons and come out!

00:14:16.808 --> 00:14:17.740
Damn it!

00:14:26.218 --> 00:14:29.551
Huh? Mr. Yamamoto.
And Yuriko, too.

00:14:29.855 --> 00:14:30.787
Captain!

00:14:31.323 --> 00:14:33.655
Captain, you accepted their deal?

00:14:33.859 --> 00:14:35.417
No talking without permission.

00:14:37.729 --> 00:14:41.256
Captain Tylor, will you
surrender to me as promised?

00:14:41.566 --> 00:14:46.026
I will. And you'll give us
the vaccine in exchange, right?

00:14:46.238 --> 00:14:47.603
Don't worry.

00:14:56.848 --> 00:14:58.406
Okay, looks good to me.

00:14:58.917 --> 00:15:03.718
Now I can surrender without
worrying. Do what you want.

00:15:04.089 --> 00:15:05.420
What we want?

00:15:10.262 --> 00:15:10.956
Don't move!

00:15:13.265 --> 00:15:14.061
Keep back!

00:15:14.366 --> 00:15:16.129
What are you doing, Harumi?

00:15:16.601 --> 00:15:20.059
You won't have the captain!
Leave the vaccine and go back!

00:15:21.873 --> 00:15:24.171
So, the android is a traitor.

00:15:24.342 --> 00:15:26.139
She's an android?!

00:15:26.411 --> 00:15:27.935
I... I don't believe it!

00:15:28.613 --> 00:15:29.637
Come on!

00:15:30.548 --> 00:15:32.379
Go ahead and kill me.

00:15:32.884 --> 00:15:34.909
But they'll destroy the vaccine.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:44.226
What will you do? Kill me and
everyone on the Soyokaze dies!

00:16:11.823 --> 00:16:14.587
Looks to me like you're a
defective piece of equipment.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.425
I'll destroy you right here!

00:16:17.963 --> 00:16:19.191
Hold it! Time out!

00:16:19.531 --> 00:16:20.259
Captain!

00:16:23.635 --> 00:16:27.731
If you're gonna destroy her,
you don't need her, right?

00:16:28.206 --> 00:16:28.968
Of course.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:30.901
Then it's simple!

00:16:31.609 --> 00:16:36.308
You think you can let us have
Harumi along with the vaccine?

00:16:36.614 --> 00:16:37.945
Wha- What?!

00:16:38.249 --> 00:16:43.516
Harumi may be an android spy,
but the Soyokaze needs her.

00:16:44.122 --> 00:16:47.057
Especially now, since our doctor
can't handle this alone.

00:16:47.359 --> 00:16:49.623
Can't you just let us have her?

00:16:50.362 --> 00:16:52.922
She's an android designed
to be a secret agent.

00:16:53.164 --> 00:16:56.292
You won't get any secrets
about our empire out of her.

00:16:56.601 --> 00:16:59.593
Fine, fine.
Wouldn't dream of trying.

00:16:59.871 --> 00:17:02.897
Please, on behalf
of the entire crew.

00:17:03.408 --> 00:17:04.534
I beg of you!

00:17:07.012 --> 00:17:08.070
Captain...

00:17:09.881 --> 00:17:14.284
Captain... To feel such
kindness for an enemy spy...

00:17:14.786 --> 00:17:19.189
I've been totally
wrong about him!

00:17:20.291 --> 00:17:21.485
Oh! That's right!

00:17:23.194 --> 00:17:24.821
Since you're giving us Harumi...

00:17:25.063 --> 00:17:27.827
...why not take my first officer,
Mr. Yamamoto, as a bonus?

00:17:29.067 --> 00:17:30.830
Wha- What?!

00:17:31.002 --> 00:17:34.768
Come on, Mr. Yamamoto!
Let's be prisoners together!

00:17:36.374 --> 00:17:40.712
You... You want me to be
a Raalgon prisoner, too?!

00:17:40.712 --> 00:17:41.371
Sure!

00:17:43.314 --> 00:17:47.546
B-B-But, I need to run
things here after you leave!

00:17:47.852 --> 00:17:49.683
Children can grow up
without parents.

00:17:49.888 --> 00:17:53.654
And a ship can sail without
a captain. Don't worry!

00:17:53.858 --> 00:17:55.086
But, sir!

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.491
Aren't you interested in seeing
what the Raalgon Empire is like?

00:17:59.764 --> 00:18:02.198
Well, yes, but!

00:18:03.034 --> 00:18:07.232
He actually believes he'll come
back from the Empire alive!

00:18:14.779 --> 00:18:18.977
Very well! I'll accept
your deal, Captain.

00:18:19.384 --> 00:18:21.284
Oh? And what about Harumi?

00:18:21.786 --> 00:18:24.016
Defective equipment.
You can have her.

00:18:24.789 --> 00:18:25.949
All right!

00:18:26.791 --> 00:18:28.383
And what about me?

00:18:28.693 --> 00:18:30.558
Defects and incompetents
don't interest me.

00:18:31.429 --> 00:18:32.521
Incompetents?!

00:18:33.698 --> 00:18:36.963
Harumi! Now you really
are a part of the Soyokaze.

00:18:37.469 --> 00:18:38.663
Captain Tylor...

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:52.075
Captain! Captain Tylor!

00:18:56.788 --> 00:19:00.724
Captain, you gave
me a human heart!

00:19:01.459 --> 00:19:05.555
I, an android, now know
about laughter and tears!

00:19:05.797 --> 00:19:07.355
Because I met you!

00:19:08.099 --> 00:19:10.431
Because in all the
time we spent together...

00:19:10.502 --> 00:19:13.596
...I learned how wonderful
a human heart can be!

00:19:16.508 --> 00:19:19.136
Captain, I think that l...

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.464
CAPTAIN!

00:20:02.387 --> 00:20:05.481
I imagine you're angry
with me, Captain Tylor.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.654
I apologize for using
such underhanded methods.

00:20:09.027 --> 00:20:14.693
But, had I not, I doubt we'd
have had a chance to meet again.

00:20:15.099 --> 00:20:16.532
I'm not mad at you.

00:20:16.901 --> 00:20:21.133
Can't see why the Raalgon Empire
doesnâ€™t just use invitations...

00:20:21.272 --> 00:20:22.762
...but I'm glad to be here.

00:20:23.208 --> 00:20:27.508
Then allow me to formally
invite you to the Raalgon Empire.

00:20:28.046 --> 00:20:30.537
Really? Say, you
got hot springs there?

00:20:31.716 --> 00:20:35.447
You'll see for yourself.
All right, take him away.

00:20:36.754 --> 00:20:39.848
If you're gonna invite someone,
you should treat them nicely.

00:20:50.101 --> 00:20:53.867
Shia Has, you've
successfully captured Tylor.

00:20:54.472 --> 00:20:55.598
Well done.

00:20:56.241 --> 00:20:57.538
It was nothing.

00:20:57.875 --> 00:21:01.003
By the way, what is
your opinion of Tylor?

00:21:01.613 --> 00:21:04.639
If he was my subordinate,
I'd get rid of him.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.613
If he was my commander,
I'd cut my own head off.

00:21:10.855 --> 00:21:15.417
Don't you think your opinion of
him is a bit too narrow-minded?

00:21:16.227 --> 00:21:20.994
I'll admit that Tylor
is not an ordinary man.

00:21:21.532 --> 00:21:23.796
He appears to be a
fool at first glance...

00:21:23.968 --> 00:21:28.735
...but I suspect there's quite
a bit of method to his madness.

00:21:29.507 --> 00:21:31.907
He's an incredibly dangerous man.

00:21:32.176 --> 00:21:34.235
And I suspect the admirals in...

00:21:34.312 --> 00:21:37.804
...the United Planets Space
Force think just as you do.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:42.849
